-Sessions never expire.
+## Session expiry
+
+Each saved session is stamped with an `issued_at` timestamp. A session older than
+`SESSION_TTL` (3600 seconds) is rejected on restore with `SessionError`, as is one
+stamped in the future. `purge_expired()` removes expired entries from the on-disk
+cache and is called on every `load_session`.
+
+Resume blobs and cache entries are base64-encoded JSON, not pickle, because the
+blob comes from the client.
